      "date": "2026-11-24 00:37:38.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\nTested on an el9.7 server (kernel 5.14.0-611.42.1) with loop-backed arrays. The mirror is md raid10 n3 with a 512K chunk. The parity array was md raid6 8+2 with a 128K chunk, and then a live raidkm 8+2 with a 128K chunk, once plain and once with --lost-list=stash-meta. 17 of 17 cases pass with each parity array:\n\n- dm-linear mirror + parity: stride=32 stripe_width=256 are set, and there is no warning when the layout is aligned.\n- A parity segment off a row warns: off in the dm table, off in its array, on an md partition, in an LVM linear LV, and in the same LV with dm-cache attached. Only the bad segment is named (3-segment case).\n- A mirror/parity boundary off a block group warns, with the parity segment first or last.\n- Mirror + plain disk, and dm-striped, are not seeded, as before.\n- A plain parity array is seeded as before.\n- mount.lustre warns when the stripe_width does not match the row of the parity segment.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
