        "committer": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-24 00:37:19.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20564 utils: probe md geometry under dm-linear OSTs",
        "message": "LU-20564 utils: probe md geometry under dm-linear OSTs\n\nmkfs.lustre gave up on a device-mapper device with more than one\nslave, so a hybrid OST (LU-20924), a dm-linear device with a mirror\nfor the ldiskfs IOPS groups followed by a parity array for the data,\ngot no stride/stripe_width.  mke2fs then took them from the stacked\nio_min/io_opt, which gives the mirror's chunk as the stride, and no\nstripe_width at all on flash.  Unaligned 1MiB writes on the parity\narray are partial-stripe writes.\n\nFor a dm device whose targets are all linear, read the table with\nthe DM_TABLE_STATUS ioctl and take the geometry from the parity\nsegments (raid4/5/6 or raidkm), skipping mirror, raid0 and plain\nsegments.  All parity segments must have the same geometry.  Since\nmballoc aligns to fs block 0, warn at mkfs about each parity segment\nthat does not start a whole number of rows from a row boundary of its\narray, following its offset through partitions and dm-linear layers\ndown to the array.  Also warn about each boundary between a parity\nand another segment that is not on a block group boundary, since\nmke2fs -E iops= marks only whole groups.  The mount-time stripe check\nuses the same probe, so it now also checks such devices.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I81623ade4a1796893615155f392b33909c06e80e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
